A NOTE ON `aliases_src/`, ADDED 2026-09-13
------------------------------------------
`ja.tsv` (16,809 rows) is listed above under "LOINC Linguistic Variants", and
that attribution cannot be correct: LOINC publishes 22 linguistic variants and
Japanese is not one of them. The file's content is organisms, disorders and
procedures rather than laboratory tests, and the build-time lexicon
(`indicator/fhir/embeddings/lexicon.py`) records it as a UMLS MRCONSO
derivation (MSHJPN / MDRJPN). Only 1.3% of its rows produce a LOINC code, yet
removing it costs 1.2 points of coverage on the 7,354-case evaluation
(0.963 to 0.951), so it stays until a curated replacement covers what it
answers. Treat its attribution as unresolved, and rest on section 1 (UMLS)
rather than on LOINC for it.

The remaining language files are being re-verified against the LOINC
LinguisticVariants they claim, one file at a time. Until each is confirmed,
treat this row as asserted rather than audited.

The per-file NOTICE documents next to the bundles carry the full reproduction
statements; this file lists the upstream licenses those statements rest on.


